        "text": "Subsecciones de: Chapter 12: Managing Containers with Docker\nP\u00e1ginas: 466-491\n\u2022 Technical requirements  (466)\n\u2022 Understanding Linux containers  (466)\n  \u2022 Comparing containers and VMs  (467)\n  \u2022 Understanding the underlying container technology  (468)\n  \u2022 Understanding Docker  (470)\n\u2022 Working with Docker  (473)\n  \u2022 Which Docker version to choose?  (473)\n  \u2022 Installing Docker  (473)\n  \u2022 Using some Docker commands  (476)\n  \u2022 Managing Docker containers  (478)\n\u2022 Working with Dockerfiles  (484)\n  \u2022 Building container images from Dockerfiles  (485)\n\u2022 Deploying a containerized application with Docker  (487)\n  \u2022 Deploying a website using Docker  (487)\n\u2022 Summary  (490)\n\u2022 Questions  (490)\n\u2022 Further reading  (490)\n12\nManaging Containers\nwith Docker\nIn this chapter, you will learn about one of the most well-known tools for creating and managing\ncontainers \u2013 Docker . The topics in this chapter will prepare you for the future of Linux, as it is the\nfoundation of every modern cloud technology. If you wish to remain up to date in a constantly changing\nlandscape, this chapter will be the essential starting point for your journey.\nIn this chapter, we\u2019re going to cover the following main topics:\n\u2022I Understanding Linux containers\n\u2022I Working with Docker\n\u2022I Working with Dockerfiles\n\u2022I Deploying a containerized application with Docker",
